  "raw_text": "iness I can only explain the taste of a Wendy's classic triple as happiness texture is very firm reminds you that you're eating a piece of meat the buns are very soft the lettuce is crispy the tomatoes aren't soggy and the onions taste like onion Agent: That sounds delicious. What are the top two or three things that make the Wendy's Classic Triple \"perfect\" for you? User: The size of the sandwich is a very hearty sandwich. If I eat one sandwich, I won't need to eat another one. Also, the ability to add mustard to the sandwich. I like mustard on my hamburgers, so it makes it better. And if you get the combo, the burger pairs well with the fries, and a small order of spicy chicken nuggets won't hurt either. Agent: Okay, I understand. On the flip side, what are the top two or three things that would make the Wendy's Classic Triple \"bad\" for you? For example, if it were soggy, dry, cold, under-salted, too greasy, or stale? User: Stale buns. Tomatoes that are old. Wilted lettuce. But I don",
